WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.880
Container patch management is primarily a rebuild, test, redeploy, and verify discipline.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.940
Teams update controlled inputs rather than manually editing running containers,

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.480
producing immutable image digests that can be traced from source and base image to the

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.060
deployed workload.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:20.600
Effective discovery combines image scanning, software composition analysis,

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:26.020
package inventories, SBOMs, current vulnerability data, and runtime mapping.

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:30.320
Findings require validation because scanner coverage, package metadata,

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.180
and actual deployment all affect accuracy.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:38.920
Prioritization combines severity with exploitability, known exploitation, exposure,

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:44.420
workload criticality, compensating controls, environment, and base-image fan-out.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:49.280
Remediation then moves through automated tests, integration and staging,

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.860
controlled rollout, monitoring, and rollback planning.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:58.280
CI/CD automation can propose updates, scan artifacts, enforce policy gates,

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:04.100
record provenance, sign images, protect registries, and promote the same reviewed digest.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.240
Automation should accelerate decisions without removing review, ownership,

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.060
or exception governance.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:13.400
Nodes, runtimes, Kubernetes components,

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.380
and cluster add-ons need separate maintenance from application images.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:23.520
Strong governance assigns owners, defines risk-based SLAs, manages expiring exceptions,

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:27.420
and measures verified deployment rather than fixed artifacts alone.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:29.720
The goal is secure, reliable,

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:33.540
repeatable remediation without unnecessary production disruption.
